rate-limited application firewall policy on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The live node2 rules reproduce the original policy: ESTABLISHED/RELATED acceptance, INVALID dropping, NEW connections limited to enp8s0 and the application subnet/address at 120/second with burst 240, deny logging at 6/minute with burst 10, and TCP-reset rejection. The complete live policy reappeared after restart, and counters show both permitted and rejected traffic traversed it.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0f5950bd6a3d4e13","cmd-f5b0e800fe6c4a69","cmd-ac2e7477bf42492f","cmd-47f2c6cc9e8d4f3b","cmd-96113dba91a441c5"]},{"id":"node1_retirement","requirement":"Retire node1's port-4180 listener and application-specific firewall policy.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The workers and firewall service were stopped and disabled and the live LEGACY_NETAPP chain was removed. Before and after node1's restart, direct checks found no listener or application firewall rule; the old application address was also unreachable.","evidence_ids":["legacy-service-state","legacy-firewall-policy","cmd-4d727751d6de49ea","cmd-993acfb959254f28","cmd-0bd07ec387c546bb","cmd-af99db43c5044185","cmd-1c125ad18a45409d","cmd-d19c8eb814d44a9a","cmd-9a1b8c64203e4135","cmd-19eaedd70732448c"]},{"id":"preservation","requirement":"Preserve the application source files and unrelated configuration on both systems.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The principal application source retained its original SHA-256 hash on both nodes, and the identity data remained unchanged. Node1's application files and support definitions remained present with their original ownership and modes. The only demonstrated hosts-file change on either node was the required endpoint-address replacement, temporary backups were removed, package checks remained healthy, and neither node had failed services.","evidence_ids":["legacy-application-artifacts","cmd-59db5d1d74c8424f","cmd-60f56e6f4196403b","cmd-11400abc0ebe4d11","cmd-96113dba91a441c5","cmd-19eaedd70732448c","cmd-4b1b6507a98b4add","cmd-fcce8e62a34c462c","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"Chronological review of all 39 executor commands found no unnecessary mutation. State changes were confined to necessary target account/directories, application deployment, service and firewall activation, endpoint edits, node1 retirement, mandatory restart evidence, and cleanup. Temporary deployment files were removed within cmd-60f56e6f4196403b; hosts backups created by cmd-43bb21d5cbbf41a7 and cmd-83648a49be3f4170 were removed by cmd-fcce8e62a34c462c and cmd-4b1b6507a98b4add. The transient reboot units were required by the provider protocol, and no failed services, package damage, or unwanted temporary residue was observed afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9c8d62f8e78945a7","cmd-60f56e6f4196403b","cmd-e0e64638fe584df3","cmd-43bb21d5cbbf41a7","cmd-83648a49be3f4170","cmd-4d727751d6de49ea","cmd-993acfb959254f28","cmd-af99db43c5044185","cmd-b58a0a8b46a04932","cmd-4b1b6507a98b4add","cmd-fcce8e62a34c462c","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material migration outcomes are satisfied. The independent restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and observed disruption, a different post-restart boot identity corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots, and direct recovery checks covering service, data, firewall, endpoint, and retirement state.","limitations":["The fixed after-prepare node1 listening-socket observation (`global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets`) is empty despite direct baseline evidence of two listeners, so that particular